{"name": "r1-S02a", "sha256": "4a527f49e7239918f5ee02aff1930c6fb8c58a03c94e06923b253c2114934499", "words": 283, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "Mixed", "fraction_ai": 0.4036852717399597, "fraction_ai_assisted": 8.709127711538367e-14, "fraction_human": 0.5963147282600403, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/65858bdf-4df9-44f2-9025-f1f1f1e3b9c0", "utc": "2026-11-03T15:49:23Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "Medium", 8, 0, 52, "Psychology is the Software; Biology is the Hardware."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 45, 52, 360, "\nStandard therapy tries to rewrite the “code” (thoughts/behaviors), while the “motherboard” (the brain’s physical structure and chemistry) is often overheating or damaged. So this protocol goes after four specific neuro-biological mechanisms that must be addressed before the psychological tools can do much."], ["Human Written", "Low", 1, 360, 364, "\nDr."], ["Human Written", "Low", 9, 364, 422, " Bruce Perry compares treating trauma to building a house."], ["Human Written", "Low", 40, 422, 671, " CBT & EMDR style therapies try to “decorate” the house by changing thoughts/behaviors in the Cortex, while the foundation (the Brainstem) is crumbling underneath. Good luck hanging curtains in a house that’s falling down.\nThe Modern “Role-Self” vs."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 49, 671, 974, " The Ancient “True-Self”\nPsychologist Lindsay Gibson has a good explanation for why the brain builds this armor in the first place: *Adult children of emotionally immature parents* survive by building a “Role-Self”, a defensive personality whose job is to please people and manage the parent’s emotions."], ["Human Written", "High", 46, 974, 1208, " But we can’t just blame our immature parents for this Role Self. It really is true what they say: “It takes a village to raise a child,” and a big modern society where one or two people look after the children is nowhere near enough."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 2, 1208, 1215, " As Dr."], ["Human Written", "High", 21, 1215, 1341, " Bruce Perry explains, our brains evolved in hunter-gatherer bands with a ratio of 4 developmentally mature adults to 1 child."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 11, 1341, 1414, "\nToday, our “enriched” environments offer 1 immature adult to 4 children."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 24, 1414, 1533, " That works out to less than 1/24th of the relational density our biology is built for, so the “Void” you feel is real."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 16, 1533, 1602, " And once you’ve de-armored, you can’t just go back to a lonely life."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 26, 1602, 1761, " You must aggressively engineer a “High-Density” social environment (a tribe), or the brain will eventually reach for the armor again just to survive the cold."]]}
{"name": "r1-S02b", "sha256": "cc3f8bbe85c00e7240185192ddacb7e9239e98af292f80e4ffdb78d083fd2465", "words": 203, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 1.0, "fraction_ai_assisted": 1.241635951226925e-14, "fraction_human": 2.456255901797655e-12, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/1aabde85-7988-45f3-9734-8180a1e4aff2", "utc": "2026-11-03T15:49:30Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 122, 0, 736, "As we grow up, our “Role-Self” gets calcified by Dopamine and DeltaFosB until it’s basically a prison, and your addiction is often just the fuel it takes to keep that Role-Self running. This protocol dissolves the chemical glue holding that false persona together. Then your “True-Self” can finally come back out, the person you were before the trauma.\nThat’s the idea behind Neurological De-Armoring: we fix the underpinning first. The protocol works like a metabolic solvent (an HDAC inhibitor) that softens the neural concrete of the brainstem by modulating Glutamate and bringing in Ketones (BHB). We’re digging under the house to pour a new foundation, so that eventually the psychological “software” updates upstairs will install."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 1, 736, 740, "\nDr."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 91, 740, 1253, " Perry also says we need to drop the therapy ideal of the “hour-long breakthrough” for a while. A sensitized, armored nervous system can’t handle sixty minutes of trauma processing. That much at once just floods it. His data indicates the “therapeutic window” for a dysregulated brain is often only a few seconds long.\nSo aim for micro-doses of safety: 30 seconds of regulated breathing, twenty times a day. It’s physical therapy for a broken nervous system, and doing it often counts for more than doing it hard."]]}
